3.2.3 Persistence Design
The system's persistence strategy is designed to ensure both the durability of data at rest and the resilience of data in transit.
Primary Datastore: The authoritative data store is a PostgreSQL database running as a Kubernetes Deployment within the GKE cluster. It houses the structured data that has been processed from the Kafka pipeline. For production environments, this deployment would be configured to use a Persistent Volume Claim (PVC) backed by Google Persistent Disks to ensure data survives pod restarts and failures.


Durable Messaging: Apache Kafka serves as a secondary, short-term persistence layer for data in transit. When the data-ingestion service publishes a message, Kafka writes it to a durable, replicated log on disk. The message persists in the topic until it has been successfully consumed by the data-processing service and the retention period expires. This ensures that even if the processing service is down, no incoming data is lost.

